# Wave W17-AB (Route 225): scorch turf — scorched hardpan turf, crater-dust flecks: a DRY rust-ochre hardpan carrying charcoal scorch flecks and pale crater dust — baked ground, never mud: the colour is kiln-dry orange-brown, the flecks are char and dust, nothing here is wet (design: scorched crater-pocked volcanic ground; everything out here trains, including the weather). Route 225’s own ground — split from its twin Route 227’s ash ground ahead of the program by state entire (scorched hardpan underfoot vs ash fallen on hot grass — and r227’s shipped ashground stands byte-preserved by spec, so the split is also one of office: this ground converts, that biome is kept).
